# New code is Rust

A new source file is Rust. A new function, type, or module goes in a Rust file.

C or C++ is the right choice only when Rust does not fit:

- The change belongs in an existing C or C++ file. Patch that file. Do not rewrite it in Rust to make the change.
- The code has to stay C or C++ to match a binary interface, a build rule that only compiles C, or a phase that runs before a Rust runtime exists (a boot sector, early loader assembly, a header other C code includes).

When the exception applies, follow [reactos-c-style.mdc](reactos-c-style.mdc).

```text
Right: a new NTFS helper in a new Rust crate, called from the existing C driver.
Wrong: a new .c file for that helper, or a Rust rewrite of the driver to fix one bug.
```
